{"t": 1784319266.621, "run_id": "fc_sphinx_global_s2_20260717_130959", "kind": "swe_task", "tag": "frozenmem", "idx": 6, "instance": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9367", "scope": "repo:sphinx-doc/sphinx", "nc": 1, "n": 1, "exit_statuses": ["Submitted"], "judge": [{"success": true, "verified": true, "reason": "The agent correctly identified and fixed the root cause of the issue. The problem was in the `visit_Tuple` method in `/testbed/sphinx/pycode/ast.py`, which was not preserving the trailing comma for single-element tuples. The fix adds a special case to check if the tuple has exactly one element and, if so, appends a trailing comma before the closing parenthesis. The fix is minimal, targeted, and addresses the specific issue without affecting other tuple cases."}], "n_retrieved": 4, "ret_scores": [0.741, 0.739, 0.739, 0.732], "mem_chars": 2741, "n_memory": 393}
{"t": 1784319353.573, "run_id": "fc_sphinx_global_s2_20260717_130959", "kind": "swe_task", "tag": "frozenmem", "idx": 4, "instance": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9281", "scope": "repo:sphinx-doc/sphinx", "nc": 1, "n": 1, "exit_statuses": ["Submitted"], "judge": [{"success": true, "verified": true, "reason": "The agent correctly identified and fixed the root cause of the issue. The problem was that Python's `repr()` for Enum members produces ugly output like `<MyEnum.ValueA: 10>`. The fix adds a special case in the `object_description()` function to detect Enum instances and format them nicely as `MyEnum.ValueA` instead. The fix is minimal, focused, and uses the existing `enum` module import. All 109 tests pass after the change, including the specific signature formatting tests."}], "n_retrieved": 4, "ret_scores": [0.733, 0.729, 0.727, 0.714], "mem_chars": 2455, "n_memory": 393}
